--
does not uniquely resolve
--
N5008 [over.match.list], [over.ics.list], [over.ics.rank]: list-initializing a
class from a braced-init-list ranks its constructors by the element conversion
sequences; a constructor taking the elements directly (vec(int) for {7}) uses a
standard conversion, which per [over.ics.rank]/(3.1) is always better than the
copy/move constructor's user-defined conversion from the list.  CBMC previously
gave both an equal args_distance and reported "symbol 'vec' does not uniquely
resolve".  Root cause: a failed implicit_conversion_sequence attempt leaked its
user-defined-conversion rank penalty (+4) into the shared rank accumulator, so
the value constructor's identity element conversion was mis-ranked as
user-defined and tied with the copy constructor.  Same error class as the
"symbol 'codet' does not uniquely resolve" dog-food noise (std_code.h,
codet(ID_assume, {std::move(expr)})).
